// A PARENTHESISED assignment target: `(x) = 5`. `vl check` returns 0 and the emitter refuses with
// `emitProgram: assignment target is not a simple name` (`compiler/wasmEmit.vl:16437`).
// Should print 5.
//
// MECHANISM, one call wide. `emitAssign` (`wasmEmit.vl:15686`) reads `P.nodes[a.binLeft]` and
// matches it against `Ident` / `Index` / `Member`. It applies `unwrapParen` to the RHS and NOT
// to the target, so a `Paren` LHS matches no arm and falls through to the floor.
//
// The message is true about the node and false about the program: `(x)` IS a simple name, and
// the checker agrees — it type-checks the assignment and accepts it.
function f(): i32 {
  let x = 1
  (x) = 5
  return x
}
print(f())
